      "marks": 1.5,
      "stem": "Given f(x) = x³ + 3x² − 4x − 12 and g(x) = x² − 3x, the functions q(x) and r(x) that satisfy f(x) = q(x)g(x) + r(x) are:",
      "options": {
        "A": "q(x) = x + 6 and r(x) = x − 3",
        "B": "q(x) = x + 6 and r(x) = 14x − 12",
        "C": "q(x) = x² + 3 and r(x) = x − 3",
        "D": "q(x) = x + 6 and r(x) = 18x − 3",
        "E": "q(x) = x + 6 and r(x) = x² − 3x"
      },
      "answer": "B",
      "accepted_answers": [
        "B"
      ],
      "explanation_steps": [
        "Divide: (x³ + 3x² − 4x − 12) ÷ (x² − 3x) = (x + 6) with remainder 14x − 12.",
        "Check: (x + 6)(x² − 3x) + 14x − 12 = x³ − 3x² + 6x² − 18x + 14x − 12 = x³ + 3x² − 4x − 12.",
        "Answer: B."
      ],
